# The switch on a Settings toggle row, flicked.
#
# Settings > Display, because it is the section with the plainest mix of rows: two switches
# among the numbers, so the control is on show next to what it replaced. Left and Right are
# what edit a toggle, and the knob slides rather than jumping - the frames between the presses
# are the animation playing at its own speed, filmed by the harness rather than written here.
scene demo
scale 4
delay 320

config
tab settings
hold 500
key down 4
hold 400
key a
hold 900

# 12h clock: on, off, on again - the second press catches the knob mid-slide, which is the
# case a switch has to get right and the reason it turns round from where it is.
key down 3
hold 700
key right
hold 800
key left
hold 700
key right
hold 900

# And the row below it, so two switches are visible at once with the cursor on one of them.
key down 1
hold 500
key right
hold 1200
